'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 11''' was the eleventh weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on October 21, 2026 at the Nagayama Municipal Gymnasium in [[Nagayama]] — the city where the Wednesday series began in June. The show was the fall-out show for the [[G1 Climax 2026 Final]], where [[Marcus Vance]] had won the tournament and challenged [[Leoni Masua]] for [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]], and it was headlined by the completion of the Wrestling Summit contract signing — the empty chair from [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 10|Episode 10]] finally filled.

== Background ==

Three days after the Aizawa Dome, NOPW's season had a new center of gravity: Vance, the G1 winner at 8-0-1, the man who broke nine matches of silence with seven words — ''"Seventeen points. No words. One more man."'' — and then said nothing again. The storylines entering Episode 11:

* '''The Summit contract.''' Leoni had signed at Episode 10 beside an empty chair. The winner's signature was owed.
* '''The Cannon Club's last night.''' At the Final, Kengo had walked out on the Usos in a title match. The twins had left the Dome without answers. Episode 11 was the answer.
* '''Kuroshio, whole.''' KAZUKI and Daigo Kuroki had settled their grudge at the Final with the returned bow. Their first tag team match since the stable's 2017 breakup followed.
* '''The family regroups.''' Taumafa, the playoff winner and Final runner-up, made his first Strong Openweight defense since the tournament.

