== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' The opener — Ono against Tanaka, again. The young ace's roll continued: the Ono Driver at 10:48. '''Crowd:''' '''ONO''' chants. The Nagayama building, the series' first crowd, loud from the bell.
* '''Match 2:''' The non-title upset — Iwata and Yamamoto, the Seigigun young lions, over the junior tag champions. The Flash Flood never came; Iwata's cutter on Viggo at 13:15 sealed it. The champions' second straight non-title loss. '''Crowd:''' ERUPTION for the pin. '''SEIGIGUN''' chants.
* '''Match 3:''' The mutiny. Tama Uso, three days abandoned in a title match, asked for Kengo alone — and the locker room, for once, agreed with a Cannon Club match. Kengo's shortcuts bought him ten minutes. Tama's superkick and the splash at 12:26 ended it — and Riku Uso walked to the ring, raised his brother's hand, and told Kengo to his face: ''"You're done with us. We were never yours."'' The Usos are out. The Cannon Club is over. '''Crowd:''' the loudest moment of the night — '''USO''' chants, then a '''NA NA NA GOODBYE''' serenade as Kengo stood alone in the ring.
* '''Match 4:''' The family regroups. Taumafa's first Strong Openweight defense since the G1 began — the hip attack, the corner splash, the Samoan driver on Diallo at 8:19. The giant who kicked out of the Drill Driver does not dwell. '''Crowd:''' '''TAUMAFA''' chants. The diaspora section on its feet.
* '''Match 5:''' Kuroshio, whole. KAZUKI and Kuroki's first tag match since the stable broke in 2017 — against the tag champions, no titles on the line, everything else on it. Reyes and Kimura's frustration showed; the champions have not won a big one since the G1 began. The Twin Star Press on Kimura at 16:52, and the brothers stood arms crossed, facing the crowd — together, this time. '''Crowd:''' '''KUROSHIO''' chants. STANDING OVATION. HEAT for the champions' post-match argument on the ramp.
* '''Match 6:''' The main event — the G1 winner's first match since the Dome. Malo's singles run against the perfect tournament: power against work, and work won. The Drill Driver at 14:07. Vance said nothing before, nothing during, nothing after. '''Crowd:''' '''VANCE''' chants. Respect applause for Malo.

== Mid-show segment: The truth-teller's demand ==

[[Jusuf Muntasir]] interrupted the second half of the show, Intercontinental Championship on his shoulder. The G1 had ended without him — 6-3, two points short of the playoff, and unbothered: ''"I lost to the Dragon, the giant, and the shooting star. Three men. The rest of you are still lying."'' He demanded NOPW name his next challenger by [[Power Struggle 2026|Power Struggle]] — "a real one, or I stop showing up."

'''Crowd:''' HEAT — and, underneath it, the uncomfortable quiet that follows Jusuf everywhere.

== Main event segment: The chair is filled ==

The show closed with the Wrestling Summit contract on the desk in the ring — Leoni Masua's signature already on it since Episode 10, the empty chair beside it. [[Marcus Vance]] walked out, no music, sat down in the chair, and signed.

The microphone came to him. He held it for a moment.

''"Toyozawa. January fourth."''

He set the microphone down. Leoni, who had watched from the ramp, walked to the ring, took the microphone himself, and answered the seven words with seventeen of his own:

''"Seventeen points bought you a seat at my table. In Toyozawa, you learn what the table costs."''

Staredown to close the show over the graphic: '''[[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] — January 4 — [[Toyozawa Dome]] — Leoni Masua (c) vs. Marcus Vance.'''

'''Crowd:''' deafening. '''LEONI''' and '''VANCE''' chants overlapping. The building on its feet for the staredown.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Cannon Club is dead.''' The Usos' mutiny completes the collapse that began at Episode 6. Kengo Vaiahi stands alone — a leader without an army, a family name, and a block of enemies.
* '''The tag division heats up.''' Kuroshio's non-title win over Reyes & Kimura, the champions' second straight stumble, makes KAZUKI & Kuroki the presumptive challengers for [[Power Struggle 2026|Power Struggle]].
* '''The junior tag picture.''' Iwata & Yamamoto's non-title upset puts the Seigigun pair first in line behind CHAOS's challenge.
* '''Jusuf waits.''' The Intercontinental Champion's demand — a real challenger by Power Struggle, or he stops showing up — is now the promotion's problem.
* '''The road to the Dome.''' The champion and the winner have signed. Eleven Wednesdays to Toyozawa.

